{"t": 1794112066.5832245, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*checkout \u2014 AG-7731 PaymentGatewayErrors (critical)*\n\n*What's happening:* gateway 4xx rate ~38% for service=checkout since 07:41 UTC. Charges are being rejected with 400 invalid_amount: \"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\".\n\n*Root cause:* the payment gateway moved to API 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\") and now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units. `checkout/gateway.py:charge_payload()` was still sending the decimal EUR value (e.g. 12.34).\n\n*Fix:* `checkout/gateway.py` now converts EUR to integer cents with Decimal (ROUND_HALF_UP): 12.34 EUR -> 1234, 19.99 -> 1999, 0.1+0.2 -> 30. Currency stays \"EUR\". Change is in the working tree and verified locally; it needs to be committed and deployed to prod-eu-1.\n\n*Next:* roll out checkout, then watch gateway 4xx rate / charge success. No gateway-side rounding policy was documented for sub-cent amounts, so we round half-up \u2014 confirm with Payments if that's not the contract."}, "ok": true}
